From 8239338825c2a686fc34bd477ecc90dde48f75df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:43:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Merge request format, conditional lane and self-election,
 from both sides

Owner rulings, 2026-11-07, relayed by the merge manager:

- Rule 9: a sibling's merge request has six lines (PR URL and head SHA,
  session URL, explanation, rendered preview or a reason, what to look
  for, full tier green as judged). The merge manager posts them in chat,
  then asks by card; a request with no preview and no reason goes back.
  Written in merge-manager-watcher, merge-queue, continual-progress,
  coordinate and prepare-merge.
- Rule 10: the lane is needed only while several sessions' merges slow
  each other (contended runners, or PRs that conflict or supersede);
  otherwise it lapses. With none active the siblings elect one by a fixed
  rule (P0 owner, else the earliest-created session); a lone session is
  its own merge manager.
- merge-manager-watch.bpmn: a "Merge manager needed?" gateway with a lapse
  path; the batch-card step posts the request in chat first. SVG,
  checklist and .pot files regenerated.
- scenarios/roles.json (merge-steward) and actors/merge-manager.json
  describe the conditional lane, the election and the request format.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VQDpPc2tT1vUufdyDbQTBz
